.TH OC-SEARCH 1 "2026-08-07" "oc-search" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
oc-search \- search opencode conversation history with ripgrep and fzf
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oc-search
[\fIquery\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B oc-search
is a fish script that searches opencode conversation history. It dumps
session messages from the opencode SQLite database into per-session
markdown files under
.IR ~/.cache/oc-search/ ,
then lets you filter and open the cached sessions with
.BR fzf (1).
.P
The database is read from
.IR ~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db .
Only non-archived sessions are indexed, ordered by most recently updated
first. If the database does not exist, or either
.B rg
or
.B fzf
is not installed, the script prints an error to stderr and exits with
status 1.
.P
The optional first argument is used as the initial
.B fzf
query. Since
.B fzf
starts in
.B \-\-disabled
mode, typing after launch re-runs
.B rg
and live-refilters the session list.
.SS Cache
Each session is cached as a file named
.RI ID __TITLE.md
in
.IR ~/.cache/oc-search/ .
The title has path-hostile characters replaced with underscores and is
truncated to 80 characters. Each file begins with a header of the title,
session ID, and local creation time, followed by the conversation with
.B USER
and
.B ASSISTANT
role markers, per-message timestamps, and message text prefixed with
.BR "> " .
.P
A session is re-dumped when its cached file is older than the session's
update time. User messages that begin with
.B [SUPERMEMORY]
or
.B <supermemory-recall>
are skipped. A
.B .version
marker inside the cache directory tracks the cache format version; when
it differs from the script's version, all cached
.B .md
files are deleted and rebuilt.
.SS Preview
The fzf preview window (right 60%, wrapped) runs
.B rg
with case-insensitive context (3 lines around the query) over the
selected file, falling back to
.BR bat (1)
with plain style, then
.BR cat (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B query
Optional positional argument. Sets the initial
.B fzf
query. There are no command-line flags.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.B ENTER
Open the selected session file in
.BR nvim (1).
.TP
.B CTRL-O
Start the supermemory user service and open the conversation in
.B opencode
with
.IR opencode\ \-s ,
using the session ID embedded in the filename.
.TP
.B CTRL-C
Exit without selecting.
.SH EXAMPLES
Search with an initial query, then refine by typing:
.IP
.EX
oc-search vaapi
.EE
.P
Search interactively:
.IP
.EX
oc-search
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db
The opencode conversation database.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/oc-search/
Cache directory holding the
.B .md
session files and the
.B .version
marker.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rg (1),
.BR fzf (1),
.BR sqlite3 (1),
.BR bat (1)
